        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/littleville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Little, an early settler, built a store near the railroad that ran through town in 1887.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/littleville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Early sustaining industries included iron ore mining and a sandstone quarry that produced the materials for blast furnaces and buildings in Sheffield, Colbert County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://encyclopediaofalabama.org/article/littleville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Littleville is part of the Florence - Muscle Shoals Metropolitan Statistical Area known as 'The Shoals'.",
